The bundled phase I and II SyGMa rule files and GLORYx rule file are GPL-3.0.
Their source and author notices are preserved by this attribution; the full
GPL-3.0 text is in LICENSE. The files are:
  src/vp_metabolite/resources/sygma_phase1.txt
  src/vp_metabolite/resources/sygma_phase2.txt
  src/vp_metabolite/resources/gloryx_rules.csv
Sources:
  https://github.com/3D-e-Chem/sygma
  https://github.com/christinadebruynkops/GLORYx
For the SyGMa rules cite Ridder L and Wagener M, ChemMedChem 2008,
doi:10.1002/cmdc.200700312. For the GLORYx rules cite de Bruyn Kops C et al.,
Chem. Res. Toxicol. 2021, doi:10.1021/acs.chemrestox.0c00224.

The curated.json transformation set was authored for this package and is also
distributed under GPL-3.0. A rule describes a candidate transformation, not
evidence that the product forms in a particular biological system.
